{"type": "text", "timestamp": 1793897516731, "sessionID": "ses_e53608e31ffeYxgV234uos8pXT", "part": {"id": "prt_1ac9fc37b0010k6YYZ3cBGIr9b", "messageID": "msg_1ac9fb828001r5JJ9uz3XXkEH5", "sessionID": "ses_e53608e31ffeYxgV234uos8pXT", "type": "text", "text": "The direct callers affected are **BillingService** and **PaymentsService**. Both call **NotificationsAPI**, which is exposed by **NotificationsService**. NotificationsService stores data in **NotificationsRedisInstance**, so losing that Redis instance prevents delivery of their notification messages.\n\nThe configured retry policy for **NotificationsService** is **three attempts with a 250 ms backoff**, controlled by **`RETRY_ATTEMPTS`**.\n\n**The available architecture tools do not specify what happens after all retries fail.** They expose no terminal-failure behavior or destination, so I can\u2019t confirm whether the message is dropped, retained, or sent to a dead-letter queue.", "time": {"start": 1793897513851, "end": 1793897516729}, "metadata": {"openai": {"itemId": "msg_020323c1e99dc09d016aecb429c74c87d1bc4b584ff2f18fc3", "phase": "final_answer"}}}}
